paths: out of each body, run back in time in the turning frame, the Coriolis force turned round (as engine/turning.py's tables are built); J = -1.331085137e+09 m^2/s^2
  the Sun's: out to 0.667 AU from it
  the Earth's: out to 0.068 AU from it
  the tables: the Sun's paths fill 0.631 AU round it (then turn back); the Earth's are clean to 3.85e+09 m (2.6 Hill radii) and cross beyond

newton: let go beside the moving Earth (moving with the turning frame), its acceleration over 0.01 s against Newton's
